NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1083,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,3,2,4,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.0002,"rank":0.0882,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV000602","role":"target","render":{"description":"Man sees a house on fire and feels that the walls are warm, an omen that the house will burn down.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/42965","original":"2 Voorloop.\nOp een morgen ging ik naar het werk. \nDaar zag ik opeens het huis van Timp in brand staan.\nNu moet men daar zo snel mogelijk heen gaan.\nZijn de muren koud, dan komt er een dode in dat huis, zijn de muren warm, dan brandt het op.\nIk voelde dus, de muren waren warm.\nDadelijk ging ik naor de vrouw terug.\nIk zeg: \"Timp zien hoes brandt gauw op.\"\nHet heeft nog twee jaar geduurd, toen ging het.","lang":"Standard Dutch; Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV005903","role":"helper","render":{"description":"When his farm burns down, a man says he saw the house on fire long beforehand but kept quiet about it.","place":"Wessingtange","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43264","original":"Veurloop.\nJoarn leden is hier brand west. Ik huilp de boer mit alles. De man stön aal man stil te kiekn en zee:“Nôn brand e ja.”\nIk vruig:“Hou komst door bie, wat betaikent dat?”\n“t Is wol al tien joar leden”, zee e dou, “op n oavend kwam k bie hoes en dou stôn alles in lichtelaaie. k Heb dr nooit over proot, mit ganaine, man nôn brand e ja.”","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.9175,7.14444]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV007406","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Lights are seen as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of fire.","place":"Musselkanaal","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44126","original":"Lichten zaggen ze vrouger voak. \"dr brandt weer wat\", zeden ze, zel wel weer gauw n huus aan goan. Dat geleuf was algemain.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.9325,7.01528]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV013008","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that all the white houses will burn down comes true; only the white church is still standing.","place":"Bourtange","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44092","original":"Oal vrouw K. zag vrouger ale widde huuzn in Boertange brannen.\n“Zai brant aal op”, zee ze. En t oal hef nog gliek kreegn ook. Allaind de widde kerke stait dr nog.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.01,7.19028]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Wessingtange.","Find Jipsingboertange on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[52.965,7.10139],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Jipsingboertange"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1418,"rank":0.2835,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ070902","role":"member","render":{"description":"People once saw a farm on fire. But when they came closer, nothing was wrong. Later the farm really burned down.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27979","original":"Myn wiif fortelde wolris dat to Sybrandahûs - tusken Dokkum en Rinsumageast - seagen lju yn 'e nacht in boereplaets yn 'e brân. Hja hearden allerhande lûden en stemmen fan minsken. Sy gongen der hinne, mar der wie neat.\nLetter is dy plaets troch de tonger opbrând.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ088406","role":"member","render":{"description":"A man once saw a farmhouse on fire, but when he came closer, nothing turned out to be wrong. Later the farm did burn down after all.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33288","original":"yn 'e brân. 't Wie by de earste bocht as men gyng fan 'e brêge fan 'e Harkema nei Surhústerfean. Mar doe't omke der by kom, brânde 't net.\nLetter is dat spul ôfbrând.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KEMP295","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A boy is released from being a werewolf when his pelt gets burnt. His friends helped him with this unintentionally.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43420","original":"De weerwolf verlost\n\nTe Blitterswijk woonde een jonge man die de naam had des nachts uit weerwolven te gaan. Enige vrienden wilden echter wel eens bij die gedaanteverwiseling tegenwoordig zijn. Zij gingen daarom een avond naar zijn huis en zetten zich om de haard. Het ging op middernacht aan en daar niemand sprak van naar huis gaan, zweette de weerwolf water en bloed van benauwdheid. Hij wilde de deur uit, maar zijn kameraden beletten hem dit en hielden hem stevig vast.\nToen het middernacht sloeg, viel opeens een groot wolfsvel uit de schoorsteen in het vuur. De weerwolf begon te schreeuwen als een bezetene en stelde zich aan als een duivel. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ037801","role":"member","render":{"description":"A boy and a girl once saw a fire from a distance, but when they came closer there was no fire at all. A year later a fire did break out at that spot.","place":"Kollum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/23086","original":"It is jierren lyn. Ik en myn feint kommen us fan Sweagerfean. Wy moesten nei de Triemen ta. Wy roannen de Úlke-loane del by Swagerfean. Doe't wy sahwat midden op 'e loane wienen, en oer de feart seagen, seinen wy: \"Sjoch, dêr is brân!\"\nDêr woenen wy hinne en sa kommen wy op 'e Trekwei. Mar dêr wie neat to sjen. Alles wie tsjuster.\nIn jier nei dy tiid briek dêr brân út op in pleats, krekt op datselde plak, dêr't wy de brân sjoen hienen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Broek belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1089,"rank":0.159,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ011312","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Near a canal people once heard hammering, but there was nothing to be seen. Two years later a wooden house was put up there.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17751","original":"It wie yn 1888 en 't gebeurde op it Blaufallaet. Doe wie dêr noch net it greate kanael, mar noch in gewoane feart. Myn mem wenne dêr. Sy is greatbrocht woarn by in âldomke fan my op it Blaufallaet. \nSy wie sawntsjin jier, doe stie se mei har omke op in joun bûtendoar. Oan 'e oare kant de feart gong it drok op in klunderjen. Mar der wie neat to sjen. \nMem sei: \"Dêr sil op in duer wol in hûs komme.\" Twa jier letter, yn 1890, woarde dêr in houten hûs delset. Greate Marten (Kalsbeek) kom der yn to wenjen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ021110","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Two men who were born with a caul saw funeral processions now and then.","place":"Haulerwijk","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20714","original":"Hjir wienen twa, dy't mei de helm geboaren wienen: Graanstra en âlde Merk. Sy seagen nou en dan lykstaesjes.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ036404","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A fortune teller makes predictions to two men about their future work and home and warns them to be careful of loose pieces of wood on the road to avoid accidents. Her predictions come true exactly.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22875","original":"Ik wie mei Bareld de Meer nei Snits ta to monsterjen. Mei de strikel yn 'e binnenbûse, om to ûngetiidzjen. Mar wy krigen beide gjin wurk. Bareld sei: \"Sille wy even nei Lytse Kjille ta op 'e Gerdyk? Dat wie in wiersizter.\nWy der hinne.\nKjille sei tsjin my: \"Binne jo troud?\"\n\"Ja\", sei 'k.\n\"Krij dan mar safolle kaerten\", sei se. Hja hie de kaerten út it laed helle fan 'e tafel. Hja gong by in stove op, sa kom se op 'e stoel. Sa lyts wie se.\n\"Om wurk út west?\" sei se. \"Ungetiidzje?\"\n\"Ja.\"\n\"En gjin wurk krige?\"\n\"Né\", sei 'k.\n\"Mar jo hà wurk\", sei se. \"Dêr geane jo moarn of oaremoarn hinne. Dêr fortsjinje jo fiifentwintich of seisentwintich goune. Der komt ek in nije wei by jimmes. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","2 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":2},"on_success":{"chime":2,"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.7114,"rank":0.7644,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST282","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmhand is courting a farm girl. Because he suspects she can practise witchcraft, he wants to break it off.","place":"Ede","prov":"Gld.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"L.C.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13626","half":"top"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"ZEEUW056","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The man sees that the dog is the devil and has himself brought back up, after which he is cursed. He comes home ill and stays ill for a long time. He remains poor all his life.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST282","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"The girl, however, asks him to come to the sheepfold the next evening. The farmhand agrees. As he stands by the sheepfold, a white figure suddenly flies past. Right after that the farm girl appears, insisting over and over that she was not the white figure. The farmhand does not believe her.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"TINNEV065","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The group starts running. When they have stopped running, the first man tells them he saw a grijze juffer (grey lady).","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310F"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"At some point he is fed up with it and wants to wake his brother up properly. In doing so he hits him on the temple, and his brother dies. The family moves away because they can no longer cope. The linden tree has kept on blooming. The murdered boy still haunts the area.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"ZEEUW054","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"There were 3 chests, with a dog on one and on the 2nd a lion holding the key to the 3rd in its mouth, which the man has to take. He does not dare, and the woman takes leave for 100 years.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CBOEK305","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"If anyone disturbs her rest, she wrings his neck. A strong man goes to the castle she haunts at night and destroys her for good.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"LAAN005","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"There was one widde juvver (white lady) whose gown was too long, so everyone tripped over it. A ziever cut it off, and from then on things always went well for him and his family.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"ZEEUW053","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The ghost leads him through passages, doors and halls until they come to 5 chests, on which sits a big black dog that takes his breath away. He can no longer speak, and the ghost takes leave for 100 years; the man is back on the road where he was addressed, drags himself home and is dead 2 days later. Someone heard of his adventure and also tried his luck, saw a light dancing ahead of him at midnight, took fright and fled.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"KEMP314","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Things would have gone badly for him on any other day. The lady offers him the chance to dig up her money chests, which he may divide between himself, the poor and the church. The next Tuesday Drikus goes with his brother-in-law Hannes to dig up the treasure. But when Hannes says, 'Look, there sits the witch', the chests sink deeper than ever.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"LYST030","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"In return she must run naked through the church. She does so reluctantly. Later a wit wief (white woman) can be seen on the land she was given. People are convinced that the woman's ghost still haunts it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"CJ001413","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He murdered his aunt for her money and since then it has been haunted there. All this happens close to the spot where the house of strong Hearke once stood.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"CJ051004","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"As suddenly as the woman and the horse appeared, they vanish again. The man hurries home, scared to death.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘farmhand’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0310. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c3"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c3"],"stack":["c1","c3"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2226,"rank":0.7299,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBOEK477","role":"member","render":{"description":"On a wager, a farmhand must show that he dares to throw the spit into the Witte Wieven (white women) pit. He throws it and challenges the witte wief (white woman), who chases him. The farmhand jumps over the lower half of the door, horse and all. The witte wief throws the spit, which sticks in the middle post of the door.","place":"Bathmen","prov":"Ov.","year":1892,"code":null,"initials":"J.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/39631","original":"In de buurtschap Loo, op het erve Noever ging men een weddenschap aan met een knecht, dat hij het spit niet durfde gooien in de Witte-wieven-kuul; deze bevond zich daar ergens in de buurt. Hij sprong te paard en joeg derwaarts, aldaar smeet hij het spit in de kuil met de woorden:\n\nWit wieven wit\nHier breng ik oe een spit\n(of: Wat heb ie'j op oe spit?)\n\nDaarop had het wit wief gezegd:\n\nA'j zoo lang wacht\nDak mien eene schoe toeknuppe\nEn de aander toerukke\nDan zal ie'j 't gebraad wezen.\n\nDe knecht rende toen in vliegenden vaart huiswaarts, achtervolgd door het wit wief en voor de achterdeur gekomen, was de bovendeur los en de onderdeur dicht, maar het paard was nogal vlug en sprong over de onderdeur. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST279","role":"member","render":{"description":"A farmhand brings the spit to the Witte Wieven (white women). One of them chases him. The farmhand just manages to flee into a house. The axe the Witte Wief (white woman) threw lands in the stiepel (doorpost). The Witte Wief could not run faster because she had trouble with one of her shoes.","place":"Tilligte","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":null,"initials":"B.R.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13623","original":"Door ouden wordt nog van de Wit Wieve verteld, die alleen kwaadaardig waren, wanneer ze getergd werden. Zo wordt verteld dat een boerenknecht eens het spit bracht naar de plaats, waar zij woonden. Hij werd door eene der witte wieve achtervolgd, doch hem niet kon inhalen, omdat ze in de haast maar een schoen had kunnen aantrekken. Toen de knecht het huis binnenvluchtte, wierp ze hem met een bijl achterna, die in de steil (deurpost) terecht kwam.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KEUNING005102","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A white ghost that floats over a gate into the field at night turns out to be a sheep.","place":"Drachten","prov":"Fr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131150","original":"Sa ha se it yn Jistrum ek hast hâwn. Der laei njonken de hurde wei in brede mei gêrs bigroeide berm. En dêr kamen de stikken lân mei hikken op 'e daem op út. Nachts seach min hiel faek in wyt ding oer in hikke it lân yn sweven. Fansels, dat wie gjin goed spul. Fêst tsjoenderij. Mar hjir kaem ek ien, dy net oan sok spul leauwde en dy 't útmakke, dat it in drint (heideskiep) wie, dat fêst it gêrs yn de berm lekkerder foun as dat yn it lân.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_15_003","role":"member","render":{"description":"About the existence of witte wieven (white women) and the spit in the doorpost.","place":"Geesteren","prov":"Ov.","year":1979,"code":null,"initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128566","original":"H.E.: Van de witn wiew he’j doar wa mangs van heurd?\nVr.Vr.: Van de witn wiew is ok niks van woar.\nH.E.: Nee, mer te geet ok um t verhaal, he. Joa he’j hier nog zonnen beuld, zonnen witn wievnbeuld. Ne, nee, nee (door elkaar heen gepraat, ze zijn het met elkaar niet eens)\nVr. [Wolberink, Jan]: Wat hadn ze bie ouns ok zegd, oh jee no valt mie t kenneke in zee Dat stun nog moal vuur joarn in de Twentse kraant. Als ik t met ene schoen had vastgebondn, gevondn als de ander gebondn.\nA.Ve.: ... t spit nog in n stiel van n nienduur nog zitn.\nF.Ve.: t Spit brengn.","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Drachten belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0967,"rank":0.8475,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"YPFOE070d","role":"card","render":{"description":"The narrator is heading home with a few friends. On the way they meet a white girl moving quickly. She floats towards a cottage. They go to investigate. Later an old man hanged himself, and people say it was connected with this. The minister is very sceptical about the story.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12149","original":"Wite juffers\nWat ik hjir yn 'e Westerein sels sjoen ha. Dat is no lyn, ik tink sa'n fiif-, seis-, sânenfyftich jier. Myn kammeraat en ik gyngen de jûntiid om in oere of alve stadichoan nei hûs ta. Doe troffen wy in pear jongelju en dy hâlden ús oan. De man sei: 'Sjoch, wat is dêr? Dêr is in famke midden yn 'e sûkerei. By it hûs dêre is it allegearre út en tsjuster, mar hoe kin dan sa'n wyt famke der yn 't lân weze?' Doe seach ik it ek. Ik sei: 'Dan moatte wy dêr ris even sjen'. Mar dat famke avensrarde tige hurd en wy koenen sjen, dat it net gie, mar dat it sweefde. It hie de grutte sawat fan in gewoan famke, en sniewyt. Ik sei: 'No, sille wy ris sjen? …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ018012","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Three white ladies, sisters, always haunt a haunted spot. Later that place was also said to be called the 'Susterwei'.","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20251","stain":"three"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST293","role":"card","render":{"description":"A road is known as a haunted road. In the evening and at night a white woman can be seen on it, with long, silky hair. Her dress is covered with feathers. Often in the morning some of these little feathers can be seen lying on the road. Her presence seems to have a fatal influence.","place":"Holten","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"G.J.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13638","original":"Het Witte Wief van de Friezeberg\nDe weg van Rijssen naar Enter is vooral bekend als de spookweg. Vroeger liep langs de eerste helft van die weg door een rij dennen ongeveer 4 meter breed een voetpad dat door de meeste voetgangers gezocht werd om van de schaduw op de anders zoo stoffige zonnige weg te genieten. 's Avonds zou zich daar echter geen sterveling wagen, want dit pad was bij avond en nacht de geliefde wandelplaats van een witte vrouw, door meer dan één gezien. Ze was een slanke vrouw met lang zijachtig haar. Haar wit gewaad was met glanzende veeren bezet en menigmaal kon men 's morgens van die witte veertjes zien liggen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"YPFOE070b","role":"card","render":{"description":"There was once a man who went with his dog cart from Hardegarijp to Bergum. A white figure travelled with him the whole way.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12147","original":"Wite juffers\nDer wie ris in man, dy reizge mei de hûnekarre de Simmerdyk del fan Hurdegaryp nei Burgum. It wie jûn en tige mistich. Hy siet yn 'e hûnekarre en njonken him siet in wite gestalte. De hiele tiid is dy njonken him meireizge, oan Burgum ta. Dy man hat in benaud oerke trochmakke.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LYST223","role":"card","render":{"description":"Grote Kees was walking over a little bridge at midnight. Suddenly he could no longer move. Witte wieven (white women) float past him. Only when they had passed could he move again.","place":"Putten","prov":"Gld.","year":1937,"code":null,"initials":"A.W.v.G.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13487","original":"De \"Witte Wieven\" zijn hier in verhalen wel bekend. Van \"de groote Kees\" wordt verteld, dat hij ze gezien heeft. Toen hij een jonge kerel was, keerde hij eens tegen middernacht van een familiebezoek terug naar huis. Onderweg moest hij door een moerassige hei, de \"breistroet\", waar een bruggetje over een beek voerde. Midden op de brug gekomen, zag hij plotseling de witte wieven. Hij kon zich niet meer verroeren en drukte zich met de rug tegen de brugleuning. Langzaam zweefden ze nader en gingen rakelings langs hem heen over de brug. Na eenige tijd kon hij zich weer bewegen. Nat van 't zweet, \"an ieder haor hing 'n dropal\", kwam hij thuis. Ze zijn ook op de Staverense hei. Bovengenoemd persoon heeft het aldus aan een kennis van mij verteld.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"ENGELB_01_005","role":"card","render":{"description":"Men who go to the place where women have seen a wit wief (white woman) find a white sheet flapping there.","place":"Gammelke","prov":"Ov.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128373"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Garyp. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c2","object":"window","text":"Garyp"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c2","word":"three","stained":"c2"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P1","difficulty":0.7182,"rank":0.5495,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KUSTERS001702","role":"card","render":{"description":"A wreath in a bed, a sign of approaching death, cannot be pulled apart. A farmer suspects his farmhand of witchcraft, sends him to work elsewhere and throws the wreath into the baking oven. At once the farmhand is standing by the oven. After the wreath is burnt, the farmhand is freed from the devil.","place":"Nederweert","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"C.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46365","original":"Bij 'n boer was 'n krans in 't bed als teken van nabije dood. Zo'n krans was zo fijn gevlochten, dat men ze niet uiteen kon krijgen. De boer verdacht zijn knecht van die hekserij en stuurde hem voor werk naar de Peel wel 2 uur ver. Daarop stookte de boer zijn bakoven en gooide de krans daarin. Meteen stond de knecht voor hem en men moest hem met geweld tegenhouden anders was hij 't vuur in gegaan. Toen de krans verbrand was, zuchtte de knecht verlicht: \"nu ben ik gelukkig\" Hij was van de duivel bevrijd.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LINSSEN001002","role":"card","render":{"description":"When the wreaths that a farmhand has hung in a tree are burnt, the farmhand who had been sent away is suddenly back; release from the enchantment after the wreaths are burnt.","place":"Asenray","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208255","original":"Kransen in bomen. Een boerenknecht hield er eigenaardige gewoonten op na. In een boom nabij de boerderij hing hij kransen op, althans men meende dat hij dat deed, aangezien hij vaak met aandacht daarnaar keek. Men vond dit zeer vreemd en men zocht een gelegenheid om die kransen te verwijderen. Men stuurde hem met paard en wagen naar Sittard. Toen hij enige uren weg was haalde men de kransen uit de bomen en wierp ze in de \"bakoven\", die destijds bij vele boerderijen stond en diende om het eigen brood te bakken. Op hetzelfde ogenblik dat de kransen begonnen te branden stond de knecht op mysterieuze wijze voor de bakoven en wilde de kransen naspringen. Hij werd hiervan weerhouden door anderen die de oven stookten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN002605","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a black cat at midnight by means of a rim is released after the rim is burned.","place":"Baexem","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208342","original":"Volgens tweede verteller was er op Nelishof te Tungelroy een knecht die elke nacht tussen twaalf en een uur afwezig was. Door een raampje ging hij naar buiten. Hij klom dan op de schansenhoop en kwam er als kat af. De boer had hem bespied en gemerkt dat boven op de schansenhoop een velg lag van een karwiel. Die had de boer daar niet neergelegd en hij zocht verband tussen de spokerij (zwarte kat) en dat karwiel.\nDit zou hij vernietigen als de knecht afwezig was. Op zekere dag had hij hem met schapen naar Antwerpen gestuurd. Toen hij een dag weg was stak de boer zijn bakoven aan en wierp de velg erin.\nOp hetzelfde moment verscheen de knecht en wilde de oven in. Het gelukte slechts met drie man om hem daarvan te weerhouden. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LINSSEN003405","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand goes at night to a belt hidden in a tree; when the belt is thrown into the fire, the farmhand, who should be far away, is present.","place":"Horn","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208417","original":"V Een knecht van de Donk klaagde bij de boer dat zijn medeknecht er 's nachts vaak op uitging en zodoende zijn nachtrust stoorde. Men ging er eens op letten wat hij 's nachts uitvoerde. Men bespiedde hem. Op een nacht zag men dat hij naar Petite-Nak, een weiland, ging waar knotwilgen stonden. Bij een van deze knotwilgen bleef hij staan en reikte met zijn arm in de holle stam. De boer stuurde deze knecht op een morgen naar de Peel (Meyel) om turf. Intussen ging men naar de knotwilg en haalde daaruit een leren riem. De boer wilde die tijdens zijn afwezigheid verbranden, maar juist toen hij de riem in het vuur wilde gooien stond de knecht, die eigenlijk in Meyel moest zijn, in levenden lijve voor hem en wilde hem verhinderen de riem te verbranden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is a profession.","Begins with F. 8 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"fddfe1195edc1e48","accepted_hashes":["2527c98dae5c4dd033048a10bc0b57518a8f2b56e0e643c7a633a4dd9a94a044","57e2ab333b6d054a7387be551573489b26231560c499123c162dce62b5159f25","6cf81cac92458b1419668d42c68236de1b62e2d630c5d71e5b3f995be2e3814f","b6ba223441efe6c110961aa35e6246e0f487b5275758affda5463e36b26a06a4","cd5322dca45120f851d0976899774b52db6ecee0ff1f8a36d100307ac8116185","daef31e372260d52ee779c064397eba81ed2d5368254dd9c85085577f830e2f9","ed8c1c07eb719c06c181dac46d225b284876f46bf4072ad105a50ce6c133b840","f6ed1ba0f8ed2c8480f4eb8d11106fc9c89c94498a6760a1838b7d29fde0bf72","fc1474744c0928fbab3495618b3d625af2ab29947626ff35f2c973fc3dd25caa"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0698,"rank":0.4838,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KOOIJMAN0294","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"General fear of the white lady.","place":"Ameide","prov":"Utr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50995","original":"DE WITTE JUFFROUW\n\nBij 't Slot had je de witte juffrouw. Veel mensen waren d'r bang van. Maar m'n vader, dat was vroeger een stroper, ok van de armoei....werken van donker tot donker....en dan 's-avonds weer op stropen uit....maar die was niet bang van de witte juffrouw!","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ090105","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven brothers is a werewolf. One of seven sisters is a nightmare. A nightmare enters the house through the keyhole.","place":"Twijzelerheide","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33428","original":"Fan sawn jonges is ien in wjerwolf.\nFan sawn famkes is ien in nachtmerje.\nIn nachtmerje komt troch 't kaeisgat yn 'e hûs.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ019728","role":"member","render":{"description":"Of seven brothers, one is often a werewolf, usually the eldest or the youngest. Such a werewolf has the nature of a wild animal.","place":"Sweagerbosk","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20528","original":"Fan 'e sawn bruorren is faek ien in wjerwolf. It is de âldste of de jongste. Hjir wie sa'n húshâlding. Dat wie Lammert Roek. De jongste, seinen se, wie in wjerwolf. Sa'n wjerwolf hie de natuer fan in wyld dier.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ041909","role":"member","render":{"description":"The eldest or the youngest of seven successive daughters is a nightmare. With seven sons, it is a werewolf.","place":"Twijzelerheide","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/23774","original":"Fan ien fan 'e sawn dochters, dy't op elkoar folgje, sûnder jonges der tusken is de âldste of de jongste in nachtmerje. Fan ien fan 'e sawn soannen is ien in wjerwolf.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Ameide belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0236,"rank":0.3077,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ044011","role":"door","render":{"description":"One of seven sons is a werewolf. You must never quarrel with a werewolf, because then he will kill you. A girl always did sewing at other people's homes. Her suitor once asked her for a handkerchief. She gave it to him, and outside he tore the thing to shreds. After that he was normal again. He turned out to be a werewolf. Then the girl broke it off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24049","original":"Ien fan sawn soannen wie in wjerwolf. As in wjerwolf jin kriget, makket er jin dea, seinen se froeger tsjin ús. Men mat der noait rûzje mei krije, sei in muoike yn 'e Westerein, dan pakke se jo.\nMyn wiif hat in kammeraetske hawn, dy naeide altyd by oare minsken. Dy hie forkearing mei in feint.\nOp in kear wie er by har, doe frege er har om har bûsdoek. Hja hie him de bûsdoek jown, mar doe hied er dy bûsdoek yn alle moster forskuord bûtendoar.\nLetter wie er wer goed west, mar 't is wol útrekke tusken dy beiden. Hwant hy wie in wjerwolf.\nHja hat it sels oan myn wiif forteld. Dat kammeraetske wenne oan it Wyldpaed.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL001024","role":"card","render":{"description":"People who do not touch werewolves; a man who is out as a werewolf is in two places at once; werewolves wear a skin.","place":"Opheusden","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209732","original":"Gaart en Stoffel van Brenk konden weerwolven. Als deze en ook andere personen daarmee bezig waren, moest men ze niet “omlegge” op het bed, want dan ging het mis met hen. Mensen zagen \"Stomp\" onder de noteboom liggen, maar ook lag hij thuis op bed. Hij was toen aan het weerwolven. Weerwolven hadden een vel om.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1182","role":"card","render":{"description":"There used to be a woman in Blokland who claimed that every evening between half past ten and twelve she heard the werewolf raging outside.","place":"Blokland","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72678","original":"De weerwolf, de weerwolf. Nou je 't zegt. D'r woonde vroeger in Blokland een vrouw. Die woonde daar op d'r eige alleen. En die vrouw die beweerde, ze hoorde iedere avond de weerwolf buite tekeergaan. Iedere avond tusse half elf en twaalf uur. Ze sloot alles d'r voor af.","lang":"Utrecht dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c1","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c2"},"stack":["c2","c3","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":4,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.7262,"rank":0.625,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ028904","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Two farmers are going to milk the cows early in the morning when one of them sees a figure walking on the other side of the ditch. The farmer's greeting is not returned: it is a ghostly apparition that disappears as suddenly as it appeared.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0475","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21852","original":"Hjir yn Stiensgea wennen twa âlde feinten, dat wienen Albert en Ate. Dy wienen boer. Sy dienen alles togearre. Se hienen lân yn Surhuzum.\nAlle moarnen gongen se mei in jok mei amers op 'e nekke to melken. Sy gongen de reed by de skoalle del.\nOp in kear, doe wienen se noch mar in lyts eintsje fuort, doe seach Ate dat der ien flakby op 'e oare kant fan 'e sleat mei harren opstapte. Ate sei: \"Goeije morgen.\" Mar dy oare sei neat werom. Albert sei tsjin Ate: \"Hwat biseistû: goeije morgen.\" \"Seachstû dan neat?\" sei Ate.\nAlbert hie neat sjoen en de gestalte wie wer fuort.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ046305","role":"variant","render":{"description":"At night a man sees a little old person approaching. When he greets the little woman, she does not greet him back. When the man looks after her, she has suddenly vanished. It is a ghost woman.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0475","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24417","original":"'t Wie feest by Bouke Pultrum yn 'e Houtigehage. (dat wie de kastlein). Myn styfheit moest de moarns ier en bitiid it hynder fan syn broer út it lân wei helje.\nDoe seach er in âld-minske oankommen.\n\"Ik tocht,\" sei er, \"hwat is dy hjir bitiid. Ik sei: - Goeije morgen, - mar hja sei neat werom. Ik sei noch us - Goeije morgen - , mar sy sei wer neat.\nDoe't se my foarby wie seach ik skruten achterom. Sy woarde samar wei yn 'e Brantsdobbe en ik haw har noait wer sjoen.\"\nSûnt dy tiid is er bang woarn. Hy doarst letter noait wer allinne yn syn eigen wein to sliepen. Hy moest altyd ien by him ha.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ101901","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Tsjerk always told stories about haunting. One evening he had to go through a gate. There he saw a little old woman. He asked who should go first: he or she. At that moment the little woman vanished as if she had never been there. It was a ghostly apparition.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0475","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37086","original":"Tsjerk Kooistra kaem wolris by ús âlden to jounpraten, en dan hied er it in bulte oer spoekjen.\nHy fortelde op in kear, hy soe ris op in joun to praten. Hy moast troch in hekke hinne. Doe stie dêr in âld minske by dy hekke. Hy seach fuort wol dat it net doogde, mar hy sei tsjin har: \"Hwa mat der earst troch: ik of jo?\"\nMei't er dat sein hie wie se fertrokken, as wie se weifage.\nTsjerk hie har net wer sjoen. 't Hie in forskining west. Dit gebeurde yn Surhuzum.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Friesland a time of day was mentioned: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1967.","That card names a time of day. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"fddfe1195edc1e48","accepted_hashes":["4411df71b6ffd8b948906fcb51d6f0a70f17982a50660c69db7226d492155816","7255610801d66774d964093c7c8e5a8084fef0f6616d9967d186df90e346486f","ac57b952469a0104880dfff367fe0c757047fd51139799529e9318193b61ec57","b983d4cf0ed75a9fbbef96b5becc1fca033ba2f511f90817a879965a75561c99"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.567,"rank":1.3,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ053402","role":"member","render":{"description":"It sometimes happens that a dead person cannot find rest because a promise made to him was not kept. If the minister addresses the dead about his unfulfilled wish and that wish is then fulfilled, the dead finds rest. If something still has to be handed to the dead, you must roll it up in a handkerchief and hold the corner of the handkerchief. If you do not do it this way, your skin will be scorched off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25362","original":"It gebeurt soms wol us, dat ien dy't to hôf brocht is de rêst net fynt. Dan komt er wer. Meastal mat er dan hwat ha. De doomny freget him dan wol faek hwer't er forlet fan hat. Dan neamt er dat.\nAs men him dat jowt komt er net wer.\nMar men mat goed oppasse hoe't men it him jowt. Men mat it yn in bûsdoek byelkoar rolje en in tippe fan 'e bûsdoek fêsthâlde. Sa mat men it him jaen. Oars skroeit it fel der ôf. De bûsdoek skroeit nou.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BIJLSMA006903","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"At night a minister is surrounded by dark figures, which vanish when he says that if they are of the devil they must go away and if they are of God they must come to him.","place":"Wijckel","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130636","original":"Op in nacht roun to Kipenburch allinne in dûmny op 'e wei. Hy sei: \"Zo alleen op de weg is toch vervelend\". Mar tagelyk seach er ek hwat oankommen. Hy wie by de Skearslipersbrêge, doe't der dûnkere gedaenten om him hinne strúnden. Dûmny sei: \"Als gij van de duivel komt, wijk van mij; komt ge van God, komt tot mij\". Doe wienen de gedaenten samar fordwoun.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ111728","role":"member","render":{"description":"When the dead keep wandering after their death, they cannot find rest because they did something wrong or because a promise made to them was not kept. The souls of murdered people also wander at night. A man who treated his wife badly during her life is constantly harassed by her ghost after her death.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29939","original":"Soms dwaelden der minsken op 'e paden om dy't al stoarn wienen. Dy hienen hwat útheefd en koenen de rêst net fine. Of se hienen noch in bigearte, dy't earst yn forfulling gean moest.\nEk guon dy't formoarde wienen dwelmen nachts om. Yn Kollumersweach wie in wiif stoarn, dy har man hie har min bihandele. Nei har dea kaem se hyltyd wer by dy man. Soms roun se njonken him lâns. Hy koe har net wer kwyt wurde.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ002908","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman dies in Egypte and visits her husband every day. The man fetches the minister and the woman tells the minister what she desires. The man does what the woman wants and since then there has been no more haunting.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1950,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/15731","original":"Yn Egypte wenne in man, dy syn wyfke forstoar, mar nei har dea kom se alle dagen by him. Hy helle de dûmny der by, dy't har oanspruts en frege hwat se bigearde. Oan dy dûmny joech se har bigearte to witen. De man foldie oan dy bigearte en it spoekjen wie dien.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Wijckel belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.2229,"rank":0.875,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ062011","role":"top","render":{"description":"Someone lives in Harkema, and when he comes back late from the farmer's he always meets an old woman on the path, whom he greets.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/26947","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEMP263","role":"half","render":{"description":"He says the little brother must ask the ghost what is wrong. The answer is that the young man died twenty-five years too early because of the stabbing. His soul must keep haunting all those years until the time is up. The priest orders the ghost to be shut in a separate room that may not be opened for the next twenty-five years.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ109412","role":"half","render":{"description":"The minister opens the Bible and lays a key of the house on a certain text. The next morning the key has turned towards the apple tree. A murdered child turns out to be buried there. After the child is reburied in the churchyard, the haunting stops.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ030711","role":"half","render":{"description":"One of the family members is once offered a hand out of nowhere. The barn doors also blow open by themselves.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"KEMP181","role":"half","render":{"description":"The body parts come together and form an old man. It is a ghost that keeps giving the soldier orders: that he must go to the cellar and lift a stone, and so on. The man boldly refuses and makes the ghost do everything itself. Three pots of gold turn out to be hidden in the farmstead. The spirit tells the soldier to give one pot to the church and one to the poor, and he may keep one himself, as thanks for releasing the ghost, who had been wicked in his life and exploited the poor.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"BLECOURTNB0111","role":"half","render":{"description":"Asked why it appears, the shade answers that he is her father and can only enter heaven once three more Masses have been said. After the girl has done this, her health improves.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ062011","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"She is always sweeping the path and the yard with a broom. One evening at full moon he sees the old woman standing in the yard again, leaning on her broom, although she has been dead for four months.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450","stain":"four"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘woman’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0450. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c7","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c7"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":4,"card":"c1","word":"four","stained":"c7"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
